%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b8c5f8bea1b438d4687ad9b712e77c3e, type: 3}
  m_Name: Level 1-5 Starting Cutscene
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CutsceneData
  line:
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: Some days after my return to Kalamba, my parents decided I should stay
      for a while, and later, I should go to Manila. I wanted to study with a teacher
      of the town, even though I could learn no more than multiplication, so I entered
      the village school.
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: At the time, an uncle of mine, Don Jose Alberto, returned from Europe.
      He found that during his absence, his wife had left his home and abandoned
      her children. He nervously looked for his wife and, at my mother's earnest
      request, he took her back.
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: "They went to live in Bi\xF1an. Only a few days later my aunt plotted
      with a Guardia Civil officer who was a friend of ours. She accused her husband
      of poisoning her and charged that my mother was an accomplice. On this charge,
      the alcalde sent my mother to prison."
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: "I don't want to tell the how much it hurt which we all, nine sisters
      and brothers, felt. Our mother\u2019s arrest, we knew, was unjust. The men
      who arrested her pretended to be friends and had often been our guests. Ever
      though I was a child, I didn't trust making friends. We later learned that
      our mother, who was away from us, was ill."
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: At first, the alcalde mayor believed the accusation. He was unfair
      in every way and treated my mother rudely, even brutally. Finally, he persuaded
      her to confess to what they wished by promising to set her free and to let
      her see her children. What mother could resist that? What mother would not
      sacrifice life itself for her children?
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: "Do\xF1a Teodora"
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7036c57c2506a5b43a8d94f11812db85, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: I didn't do anything wrong! I didn't poison her! I helped looked for
      her when she was missing. I was even the one to convince Don Jose to take her
      back because he was really worried!
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: Alcalde Mayor
    speakerType: 1
    hero: {fileID: 0}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: Those are just your words, but can you even provide evidence for that?
      In the scene of the crime you committed, there is poison and your sister-in-law
      is ill. We have made our decision.
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: "Do\xF1a Teodora"
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7036c57c2506a5b43a8d94f11812db85, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: You are all wrong. I never did anything wrong.
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: Alcalde Mayor
    speakerType: 1
    hero: {fileID: 0}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: We can argue about this all day and it will go nowhere. I'll make this
      easier for you. If you sign a statement then we can make it so that you're
      free to be released and you get to see your children safe in a matter of days.
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: "Do\xF1a Teodora"
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7036c57c2506a5b43a8d94f11812db85, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: Your statement is telling me to agree to the crimes that I have never
      committed. I won't sign your agreement. Leave my children out of this, they
      were never even involved in the crime I never committed.
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: Alcalde Mayor
    speakerType: 1
    hero: {fileID: 0}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: 'I won''t do anything to your children. But your children will surely
      miss you, what if you take way too long and they can''t ever see you again
      for a long time? Sign it with a signature. '
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: "Do\xF1a Teodora"
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7036c57c2506a5b43a8d94f11812db85, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: Ah... My children...
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: Alcalde Mayor
    speakerType: 1
    hero: {fileID: 0}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: "I can wait how long I want to, this does not affect me. Rot in prison,
      that is your choice. Months, perhaps even longer, Do\xF1a Teodora. "
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: "Do\xF1a Teodora"
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7036c57c2506a5b43a8d94f11812db85, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: ...
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: "Do\xF1a Teodora"
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7036c57c2506a5b43a8d94f11812db85, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: ...
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: "Do\xF1a Teodora"
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7036c57c2506a5b43a8d94f11812db85, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: Will you truly set me free and that I can go home?
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: Alcalde Mayor
    speakerType: 1
    hero: {fileID: 0}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: I give you my promise.
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: "Do\xF1a Teodora"
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7036c57c2506a5b43a8d94f11812db85, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: Fine. If it's for my children...
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: Narrator
    speakerType: 2
    hero: {fileID: 0}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: She takes the pen and signs. Her hands tremble a bit but she doesn't
      look up.
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: "Do\xF1a Teodora"
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7036c57c2506a5b43a8d94f11812db85, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: Aaahh.... my children... forgive me.
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: Narrator
    speakerType: 2
    hero: {fileID: 0}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: The Alcalde Mayor leaves without a word. The guard takes her back to
      her cell.
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 0
  - speakerName: Narrator
    speakerType: 2
    hero: {fileID: 0}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: ...
    isLeftSide: 0
    pose: 0
